A = {
90: """I remember a funny shopping experience from last year. I went to an electronics store to buy a new rice cooker, because our old one was broken. I chose a nice one, paid for it, and took it home. That evening, my wife wanted to cook rice, but when she opened the box, there was no rice cooker inside. Instead, there was an electric kettle. I was really confused at first, and then we both started laughing. The next morning, I went back to the store with the receipt and the box. The staff were very surprised and apologized many times. They said someone must have mixed up the boxes in the warehouse. They gave me the correct rice cooker and even let me keep the kettle as a gift for the trouble. So in the end, it turned out to be a lucky mistake.""",
91: """The last time I went shopping was last weekend. I went to a big shopping mall in the city center with my wife and daughter, because we needed to buy some new clothes for the cold season. First, we went to a children's clothing store and bought my daughter a warm jacket and two pairs of pants, because she's growing so fast. Then my wife found a nice sweater that was on sale. I bought a new pair of running shoes, since my old ones were worn out. What was special about that day was that there was a big promotion at the mall, so everything was about thirty percent off. We saved quite a lot of money. After shopping, we had lunch at the food court, and my daughter played at the indoor playground. It was tiring, but we all had a good time.""",
92: """In Vietnam, people usually dress quite casually in daily life, mostly because the weather is hot for most of the year. On normal days, people wear T-shirts, jeans or shorts, and sandals. Young people like to follow fashion trends, so they often wear oversized T-shirts, sneakers, and baseball caps. For work, it depends on the job. People who work in offices or banks usually wear more formal clothes, like shirts, trousers, and sometimes jackets. Many companies and factories have uniforms, so workers wear the same clothes every day. For special occasions, like weddings or Tet, people dress up more. Women often wear the ao dai, which is our traditional dress, and men wear suits or nice shirts. In winter in the north, people also wear warm jackets, scarves, and boots, because it can get quite cold.""",
93: """Personally, I prefer a simple and comfortable style. On weekends, I usually wear a T-shirt or a polo shirt with jeans or khaki pants, and sneakers. I like neutral colors, like white, gray, navy blue, and black, because they're easy to match, and I don't need to think too much about what to wear in the morning. For work, I have to wear the company uniform, so I don't need to worry about fashion during the week. When I go to a wedding or a special event, I wear a light blue shirt with dark trousers and leather shoes. Today, since I'm at home, I'm wearing a gray T-shirt, black shorts, and slippers, which is my favorite outfit for relaxing. I'm not really interested in following trends, but I do care about wearing clothes that fit well and feel comfortable.""",
94: """When I was a teenager, around fifteen years ago, fashion was quite different from now. Back then, skinny jeans were really popular, and many guys wore tight jeans with colorful T-shirts and big belts. Spiky hairstyles with lots of hair gel were also very trendy, and I had that hairstyle for a while, which is a little embarrassing now. Girls often wore long, straight hair and jeans with flat shoes. Clothes were also less varied, because most people bought them at local markets, and international brands were rare and expensive. These days, fashion has changed a lot. Loose, oversized clothes are more popular, and people care more about comfort. Young people also follow trends from social media and Korean celebrities. Plus, online shopping makes it easy to buy all kinds of styles, so fashion changes much faster than before.""",
95: """The last time I bought a new piece of clothing was about two weeks ago. I needed a new jacket, because the weather was getting colder and my old jacket had a broken zipper. At first, I went to a few shops in a shopping mall near my house, but I couldn't find one I liked in my size. The ones I liked were either too big or too expensive. So I decided to look online. I found a dark green jacket on a shopping app with good reviews and a reasonable price. The problem was that I wasn't sure about the size, so I checked the size chart and read the comments from other buyers. I ordered a large, and it arrived three days later. Luckily, it fit me perfectly, and the quality was even better than I expected. I've been wearing it almost every day since then.""",
96: """I live in the north of Vietnam, so we have four seasons, although they're not as clear as in some other countries. Spring is from February to April. It's cool and humid, and there's often a light drizzle, so everything feels a bit wet. Summer is from May to August, and it's very hot and humid, sometimes up to thirty-eight degrees. There are also sudden thunderstorms in the afternoon. Autumn is from September to November, and it's my favorite season. The weather is cool and dry, the sky is clear, and there's a gentle breeze. In Hanoi, autumn is also the season of a special flower called hoa sua, which has a strong smell. Winter is from December to January, and it's cold and dry, sometimes below ten degrees. I like autumn the most, because it's the most comfortable time to go out.""",
97: """Today the weather is really nice where I am. It's late October, so autumn is here, and the temperature is around twenty-six degrees, which is perfect. This morning it was a little cool, so I wore a light jacket when I left the house, but by noon it got warmer, and now I'm just wearing a T-shirt. The sky is mostly clear and blue, with a few white clouds, and there's a light breeze. It's not humid like in summer, so I don't feel sticky or sweaty. According to the weather forecast, it might rain a little tonight, but tomorrow will be sunny again. This kind of weather makes me want to go outside, so I'm planning to take my daughter to the park this evening. I really wish the weather could be like this all year round.""",
98: """I had an experience with severe weather a couple of years ago, when a big typhoon hit northern Vietnam. We had heard about it on the news for several days, so we bought food and water and charged our phones. When it arrived, the wind was so strong that our windows were shaking, and around midnight the power went out in the whole building. The next morning, the city looked like a disaster area. Many big trees had fallen onto the streets and cars, and some roads were flooded up to my knees. Schools were closed for two days, and many businesses, including my company, told people to stay home. People dealt with it by helping each other. Neighbors worked together to move fallen trees, and volunteers brought food to people in the flooded areas. It was scary, but it showed how strong our community is.""",
99: """I think the weather in my country has changed quite a lot since I was a child. When I was young, the seasons in the north were very clear. Winters were really cold, and I remember wearing several layers of clothes to go to school. Summers were hot, but not as extreme as now. These days, summers are much hotter and longer. Some days, the temperature goes up to almost forty degrees, and the heat waves last for weeks. Winters are also shorter and warmer than before. Another big change is that there are more extreme weather events, like strong typhoons, heavy floods, and droughts in some areas. I've also noticed that the weather is less predictable. For example, sometimes it suddenly gets cold in spring. Many people say this is because of climate change, and I think they're right.""",
100: """In Vietnam, the most common way to get around is definitely by motorbike. Almost every family has at least one or two motorbikes, because they're cheap, fast, and easy to park, and they can go through narrow streets and traffic jams. That's why you see thousands of motorbikes on the streets, especially in big cities like Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City. Cars are becoming more popular too, especially among middle-class families, but traffic jams and parking are big problems. As for public transportation, there are city buses, and recently, Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City have opened metro lines, which are clean and modern. Many people also use ride-hailing apps to book motorbike taxis or cars. For long distances, people usually take buses, trains, or planes. Domestic flights are quite cheap now, so many people fly between the north and the south.""",
101: """I usually get around by motorbike, because it's the most convenient way in my city. I ride my motorbike to work every day, and it takes about twenty-five minutes. On the way, I also drop my daughter off at her kindergarten. My company also has a shuttle bus for employees, but I prefer my motorbike because I can leave whenever I want. On weekends, if my whole family goes out, we sometimes use my father's car or book a car through a ride-hailing app, especially when it's raining. I rarely take public buses, because the bus routes in my city aren't very convenient for me. When I go to Hanoi, I sometimes take the bus, and once I'm there, I like to try the new metro line. For long trips, like going to the beach or to the south, I usually take a coach or a plane.""",
102: """When I was a child, transportation in my hometown was very different. Most people used bicycles to get around. My father rode a bicycle to work, and I rode one to school with my friends every day, even on rainy days. Motorbikes were less common and quite expensive, so only some families had one. I remember my family bought our first motorbike when I was about ten, and it was a big event. Cars were very rare. If we wanted to go to a bigger city, we took an old, crowded bus, and the trip took a long time because the roads were narrow and bumpy. These days, things have changed a lot. Almost everyone has a motorbike, many families have cars, and the roads are much wider and better. We also have ride-hailing apps, which didn't exist back then.""",
103: """I had a transportation problem about a year ago that I still remember. I was riding my motorbike to an important meeting in Hanoi, which was about an hour from my house. Halfway there, on the highway, my motorbike suddenly got a flat tire. There was no repair shop nearby, and it was really hot. I was so worried, because the meeting was in forty minutes. First, I called my manager and explained the situation. Then I pushed my motorbike for about fifteen minutes until I found a small repair shop. While the mechanic was fixing the tire, I booked a ride-hailing car on my phone, left my motorbike at the shop, and went to the meeting. I arrived ten minutes late, but luckily my manager understood. After the meeting, I went back to pick up my motorbike. Since then, I check my tires before every long trip.""",
104: """I make different kinds of appointments in my life. The most common ones are medical appointments. For example, I take my daughter to the pediatrician when she's sick and for her regular check-ups, and I go to the dentist about twice a year to get my teeth cleaned. I also have a health check-up at work every year. Besides that, I make appointments to get my hair cut at a barber shop near my house, and to get my motorbike serviced at the repair shop. At work, I often schedule meetings with my team or with other departments. As for where I go, most of my medical appointments are at a private clinic in the city center, because it's clean and you don't have to wait long. The barber shop and the motorbike shop are both close to my home, so they're very convenient.""",
105: """When I make an appointment, I usually follow a few steps. First, I check my schedule to find a free time, usually on a weekend or after work. Then I call the place or use their app or website to book a time. For example, when I book a dental appointment, I use the clinic's app. I choose the service, the date, and the time, and then I enter my name and phone number. After that, I usually get a confirmation message. To make sure I don't forget, I add the appointment to the calendar on my phone and set a reminder for the day before. On the day of the appointment, I prepare any documents I need, like my ID card or health insurance card, and I try to leave home a bit early so I can arrive ten minutes before the appointment time. If I can't go, I always call to cancel or reschedule.""",
106: """I remember an appointment with the dentist when I was about eight years old. I had a really bad toothache for a few days, so my mother made an appointment at a dental clinic in town. I was really scared, because I had heard from my friends that going to the dentist was very painful. When we arrived, the clinic smelled of medicine, and I could hear the noise of the drilling machine from the other room, which made me even more nervous. When it was my turn, I cried and refused to open my mouth. The dentist was very patient. She showed me all her tools and explained what she was going to do. In the end, she pulled out my bad tooth, and it didn't hurt as much as I expected. Afterwards, she gave me a sticker, and my mother bought me ice cream as a reward.""",
107: """Something unexpected happened with one of my appointments last year. I had made an appointment at a hospital in Hanoi for a health check-up. I took a morning off from work, woke up early, and drove for an hour to get there. But when I arrived at the reception desk, they couldn't find my name in the system. Apparently, there was a problem with their online booking app, and my appointment was never saved. I was really annoyed, because I had taken the day off. First, I showed them the confirmation message on my phone. The staff apologized and talked to their manager. In the end, they managed to fit me in, but I had to wait for almost two hours. I was tired, but at least I got my check-up done. Since then, I always call the clinic one day before to confirm my appointment.""",
108: """There are several popular holidays in Vietnam, but the biggest one is Tet, the Lunar New Year. It usually falls in late January or February. People celebrate it at home with their families, and many people travel back to their hometowns for it. Before Tet, people clean and decorate their houses with peach blossoms or kumquat trees. During Tet, families get together, eat traditional food like banh chung, visit relatives, and give lucky money to children. Many people also go to temples or pagodas to pray for good luck. Another popular holiday is the Mid-Autumn Festival, which is mainly for children. Kids carry colorful lanterns, watch lion dances in the streets, and eat mooncakes. There's also National Day on September second, when many people travel or go to the beaches, and the government organizes fireworks in big cities.""",
109: """One of my favorite holiday memories from my childhood is the Mid-Autumn Festival when I was about seven years old. I was at my grandparents' house in the countryside. In the evening, the whole village was decorated with colorful paper lanterns, and there was a big full moon in the sky. My grandfather made me a star-shaped lantern from bamboo and red paper, and he put a small candle inside it. I remember walking around the village with my cousins and other kids, holding our lanterns and singing songs. There was a lion dance group going from house to house, with loud drums, and we followed them everywhere. Later, my whole family sat in the yard, eating mooncakes and fruit, and drinking tea under the moonlight. It was such a simple and peaceful night, and I still remember the smell of the candles.""",
110: """The most recent holiday I celebrated was the Mid-Autumn Festival last month. It was memorable because it was the first time my daughter was old enough to really enjoy it. A week before, we made a paper lantern together, and she was so proud of it. On the festival night, we went to a big event in the city park. There were lots of lights, lantern displays, and lion dance performances. My daughter was really excited, and she kept dancing to the drums. After that, we went to my parents' house, and my mother had prepared a small party with mooncakes, fruit, and sweets shaped like animals. My daughter and her cousins played with their lanterns in the yard until late. What made it so special was seeing my daughter enjoy the same traditions that I loved when I was a child.""",
111: """Vietnam has quite a few holidays. The most important one is Tet, the Lunar New Year. During Tet, people return to their hometowns, clean and decorate their homes, cook traditional food like banh chung, and visit relatives to wish them a happy new year. What makes it special is that it's the only time of the year when the whole family gets together, and the holiday lasts for about a week. Another one is the Mid-Autumn Festival, which is like a children's festival. Kids get lanterns and toys, and families eat mooncakes and watch the full moon. We also have the Hung Kings Commemoration Day in spring, when people remember the founders of the country. And of course, there's National Day on September second, when there are parades and fireworks. Each holiday has its own meaning, but they all bring people closer together.""",
112: """Banks in Vietnam are quite modern these days. Most of them are located on main streets in the city center, near shopping areas or office buildings, so they're easy to find. Many banks also have small branches in residential areas and in industrial parks, like near my company. From the outside, they usually have big glass doors and a large sign with the bank's logo and color. Inside, there's a waiting area with chairs, a machine where you take a number, and a row of counters where the staff help customers. They're usually clean and air-conditioned. There are also ATMs outside almost every branch, and in supermarkets and shopping malls. However, these days, many people rarely visit the bank, because they can do almost everything on their banking apps, like transferring money, paying bills, or even opening a savings account.""",
113: """These days, I only go to the bank a few times a year, usually when I need to do something I can't do on the app, like updating my personal information or getting a new card. When I walk in, a security guard usually greets me and asks what I need. Then I take a number from the machine and sit in the waiting area. While I'm waiting, I check my phone or look at the screens showing interest rates. When my number is called, I go to the counter and explain what I need. The staff usually ask for my ID card and give me some forms to fill out and sign. Sometimes they need to take a photo or my fingerprint for verification. After that, they process my request, which takes about ten to fifteen minutes. Finally, I check everything, thank the staff, and leave.""",
114: """I remember the bank in my hometown when I was a child. My father sometimes took me there when he needed to send money to my uncle. It was a small, old building with a heavy metal door and bars on the windows. Inside, it was quite dark, and there was only an old fan on the ceiling. There were long wooden counters, and the staff sat behind glass windows. Everything was done on paper, and people had to wait in long lines, sometimes for an hour. I remember the staff counting stacks of cash by hand, which looked amazing to me. Banks today are completely different. They're bright, modern, and air-conditioned, and everything is done on computers. You take a number instead of standing in line. But the biggest difference is that now you can do most things on your phone, so you hardly need to go to the bank.""",
115: """I had a problem with my bank about a year ago. One day, I tried to pay for my groceries at the supermarket with my bank card, but the payment was declined. I was confused, because I knew I had enough money in my account. When I checked my banking app, I saw that my account had been temporarily locked. I was worried that someone had tried to hack my account. The next morning, I went to the bank to find out what happened. The staff explained that my account was locked because I had entered the wrong password three times on the app the night before. I didn't remember doing that, but maybe my daughter had been playing with my phone. They checked my ID card, asked me some security questions, and unlocked my account. Since then, I've set a better password and I don't let my daughter use my phone.""",
116: """Hello, excuse me. I'm looking for some new clothes for work and for the weekend. Could you help me, please? First, I really like this light blue shirt. Do you have it in a medium size? And is it made of cotton? I want something comfortable, because the weather is still quite hot. Also, do you have this shirt in other colors, like white or gray? Second, I need a pair of dark trousers to go with it. Could you show me where the trousers are, and can I try them on? Where is the fitting room? Oh, and one more thing. Are there any promotions right now? For example, if I buy two shirts, do I get a discount? Finally, what's your return policy? If something doesn't fit after I wash it, can I exchange it? Thank you so much for your help.""",
117: """Hello, my name is Minh. I'm calling about an order I received from your online store this morning. I ordered three shirts last week, and two of them are fine, but there's a problem with the white one. When I opened the package, I noticed that there's a big stain on the front, and one of the buttons is missing. So I can't wear it, especially because I bought it for a wedding this weekend. I'd like to suggest a few ways to solve this problem. First, could you send me a new white shirt in the same size as soon as possible, before Saturday? If that's not possible, I could come to your store this week and exchange it myself. Or, if you don't have this shirt in stock anymore, I'd like a full refund. Please call me back and let me know. Thank you.""",
118: """Yes, I remember being really unhappy with a pair of shoes I bought online about a year ago. I ordered a pair of brown leather shoes for work. In the pictures, they looked really nice and well-made, and the price was a bit high, so I expected good quality. But when they arrived, I was disappointed. The leather looked cheap, and the color was much lighter than in the photos. Even worse, after wearing them for just one week, the sole started coming off. So I contacted the shop through the app and sent them photos of the problem. At first, they only offered me a small discount voucher, which I didn't accept. Then I reported the problem to the shopping app. After a few days, the shop agreed to give me a full refund. Since then, I always read reviews carefully and buy shoes in real stores.""",
119: """Hi Lan, it's me, Minh. How are you? I heard that a new shopping center just opened near your house, and you went there last weekend, right? I'm thinking about going there with my family this Saturday, so I want to ask you a few questions. First, what kinds of stores are there? Is there a supermarket, or just clothing stores? Also, are the prices reasonable, or is it expensive? Second, I heard they're having some promotions for the opening. Is that true? What kind of discounts do they have? Third, is there a place for kids to play? My daughter loves playgrounds, so that would be great. And finally, is it easy to park there? Is there a parking lot for cars, or should I go by motorbike? Please call me back when you're free. Thanks a lot, talk to you soon.""",
}
